{
  "title": "Phantom® Fibula Nail System",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423233/phantom-r--fibula-nail-system",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Sep 18 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Phantom® Fibula Nail System is a purpose-built, intramedullary solution for distal fibula fixation that couples an expandable proximal fixation feature, a threaded distal peg cluster, and integrated targeting for rigid or dynamic syndesmotic stabilization.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A radiolucent outrigger enables reduction maneuvers and precise placement of implants through the nail.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A streamlined guide and reaming workflow helps optimize the correct start point and maintain central canal trajectory.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Implant diameters and lengths cover a wide spectrum of patient anatomies.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Implants & materials:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Type II anodized titanium implants available in multiple diameters and lengths to accommodate varied fibular canals.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Distal fixation & syndesmosis through the nail:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Threaded distal locking holes accept Ø2.7 mm headless threaded pegs that interlock with the nail to secure the distal fragment and help resist backout or migration.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Multiple syndesmotic options from the P28 portfolio include R3FLEX™, R3ACT™, or Ø3.5 mm static threaded pegs targeted through the nail at defined angles.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Proximal fixation:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Expandable proximal wings increase the nail’s effective diameter by ~1 mm per side (2 mm total) to mitigate rotation and potential fracture collapse.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "The wings can be retracted for removal.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Guidance & reaming:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Entry K-wire guide optimizes the start point and nail trajectory.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Opening distal reamer contains notches for syndesmotic levels and hash marks for countersink depth.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Solid and cannulated proximal reamers are available.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Optional curved reamer guide centralizes the pilot and avoids eccentric reaming.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Outrigger & reduction aids:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Radiolucent outrigger with clearly labeled targeting windows.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "K-wire tip hole shows nail depth.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Curved K-wire guides capture the fragment around the nail.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Locking K-wire clamp sleeve holds tibial control for rotation or traction after insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "End caps & removal:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "End caps (1, 5, 10, 20 mm) fine-tune distal position when the syndesmosis requires countersinking.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Easy-Out and removal hook provided to facilitate efficient explantation.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Indications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Fixation of fibular fractures and osteotomies.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Approach",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Positioning:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Supine with ipsilateral bump",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Lateral decubitus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Prone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Internal rotation of the leg exposes the lateral fibula and enables AP imaging.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Incision:",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "1.5–2 cm vertical incision centered over the distal fibular tip, extending slightly proximal and distal.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Soft-tissue dissection exposes the distal fibula while protecting the peroneal tendons.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
